1
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:38,080
[First Love Again]

2
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:40,840
[Episode 4]

3
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:42,240
Thank you, Senior,

4
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:44,570
for giving me one-on-one coaching today.

5
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:46,080
You've gained

6
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:47,410
some experience by now.

7
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:49,920
Are you available tomorrow
during the day?

8
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:50,600
Yes.

9
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,840
Then I'll find somewhere else.

10
00:01:52,539 --> 00:01:54,240
[Young Host Skills Training]

11
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:55,500
Won't I be taking up
too much of your time?

12
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:56,360
Don't forget,

13
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:58,120
I'm the deputy director
of the campus TV station.

14
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:58,800
How could I

15
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:00,800
pass up a promising talent like you?

16
00:02:03,770 --> 00:02:06,010
All right, head back

17
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,370
and get some rest early.

18
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:10,160
Bye-bye.

19
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:11,400
Bye.

20
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:35,200
Captain,

21
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:37,360
you've been pushing yourself
so hard these days.

22
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:38,640
Can you keep this up?

23
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,380
Ninety-eight,

24
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:43,720
ninety-nine.

25
00:02:45,050 --> 00:02:46,250
Ninety-nine...

26
00:02:46,270 --> 00:02:48,400
That's enough. Take a break, Captain.

27
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:54,840
Listen up.
The university just informed us

28
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,000
about a volunteer event

29
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,640
at a welfare home.

30
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:59,100
They'd like our basketball team

31
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:00,300
to send a few people.

32
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:02,920
Gu Han, get a few people to attend.

33
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:03,640
Okay.

34
00:03:04,620 --> 00:03:05,880
All right, dismissed.

35
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:10,120
Li Sirui, Chen Yu, Kong Fang.

36
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,470
Just you three.

37
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:14,720
So much for my Saturday off.

38
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:17,370
We've gotta follow the captain's orders,

39
00:03:17,370 --> 00:03:18,210
right?

40
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:21,480
I'll find a DJ for the event, too.

41
00:03:25,290 --> 00:03:26,079
Our campus TV station

42
00:03:26,079 --> 00:03:27,520
is visiting a welfare home tomorrow.

43
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:29,640
I think it'd be
a great learning opportunity.

44
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:30,640
If you're interested,

45
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:31,720
you can come along.

46
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:32,360
Okay.

47
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:34,160
We'll meet
at eight tomorrow morning, then.

48
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:35,360
See you there.

49
00:03:36,870 --> 00:03:38,079
I've got to go. Bye-bye.

50
00:03:38,079 --> 00:03:38,760
Bye-bye.

51
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,160
What's wrong?

52
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,160
What now?

53
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:53,880
Don't think you're off the hook

54
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:55,200
just because your research report
got approved.

55
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,920
Spend more time studying.

56
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:03,080
Come on, hurry up. I'm starving.

57
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:07,170
What's his problem?

58
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:10,380
Just put your stuff on the bus,

59
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:11,540
then find a seat.

60
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:16,240
Senior.

61
00:04:18,079 --> 00:04:19,360
-Sorry, Senior.
-Sorry, Senior.

62
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:20,040
We're late.

63
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:21,570
It's okay. Hurry and get on.

64
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:22,800
Let's go.

65
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:24,410
Watch your step.

66
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,280
Sir, everyone's here.

67
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:30,440
-Okay.
-We can leave now.

68
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:31,080
All right.

69
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:51,120
Today, as representatives
of Jiangcheng University,

70
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:52,640
we've come to Jiangcheng Welfare Home

71
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:53,620
to show these children

72
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:55,620
some love.

73
00:05:05,250 --> 00:05:06,480
Kids, would you like to see

74
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,480
some animals playing basketball?

75
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:09,840
-Yes!
-Yes!

76
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:12,720
Come with me.

77
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:14,640
Put it here.

78
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:15,300
Here you go.

79
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:18,680
Pick one.

80
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:35,600
We're just missing a host.

81
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:36,730
Want to give it a try?

82
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:39,440
It's okay.

83
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,130
You can do it!

84
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:00,280
The zoo is hosting

85
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:03,120
a one-of-a-kind basketball game today.

86
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:26,280
T-The contestants...

87
00:06:32,470 --> 00:06:34,830
T-The contestants...

88
00:06:49,250 --> 00:06:50,010
I've got you.

89
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:52,290
Just keep your eyes on me, okay?

90
00:06:59,550 --> 00:07:01,010
Come on, let's keep going.

91
00:07:04,130 --> 00:07:05,050
I'm on his team.

92
00:07:09,510 --> 00:07:10,510
The little lion

93
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:14,640
wanted to team up
with the little pink pig.

94
00:07:15,300 --> 00:07:16,260
But the pig said,

95
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:19,000
"No way!

96
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:21,380
We're not even from the same cartoon!"

97
00:07:21,380 --> 00:07:22,200
Come on, do it.

98
00:07:28,170 --> 00:07:30,850
The little lion said, "I don't care.

99
00:07:31,170 --> 00:07:33,000
No one will even notice anyway!"

100
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:43,280
"All right."

101
00:07:43,790 --> 00:07:44,990
So it crouched down.

102
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:47,520
The little lion leaped onto its back,

103
00:07:47,650 --> 00:07:49,850
and the two charged toward the hoop.

104
00:07:49,870 --> 00:07:51,390
Score!

105
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:56,140
Yeah!

106
00:07:56,890 --> 00:07:59,290
Just then, the little lamb
stepped forward

107
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:01,640
and asked the kids for help.

108
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:02,920
Who wants to join in?

109
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:06,080
-Me!
-Me! I'll do it!

110
00:08:07,290 --> 00:08:08,530
I will!

111
00:08:08,550 --> 00:08:09,990
-Me!
-Me!

112
00:08:10,020 --> 00:08:11,420
The ball's over here!

113
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:40,440
Let me help you.

114
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:52,500
Give it a shake.

115
00:09:15,370 --> 00:09:16,130
Thank you.

116
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,130
I should thank you, too.

117
00:09:32,450 --> 00:09:34,310
Why were you hiccupping just now?

118
00:09:38,230 --> 00:09:39,550
I ate too much at lunch.

119
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:53,790
What about last time
at the basketball court?

120
00:09:53,810 --> 00:09:55,010
Was it the same thing?

121
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:08,260
I've actually been like this
since elementary school.

122
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,720
Whenever I'm in a crowd,

123
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:13,700
I start hiccupping uncontrollably.

124
00:10:21,290 --> 00:10:23,960
Dear teachers and fellow students,

125
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:26,120
Happy New Year!

126
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:33,490
On this beautiful winter day,
basking in the warm sunshine,

127
00:10:33,490 --> 00:10:36,050
we gather here with joy in our hearts...

128
00:11:01,790 --> 00:11:03,390
Ever since that day,

129
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,960
whenever I host an event

130
00:11:06,170 --> 00:11:08,300
or give a speech in front of strangers,

131
00:11:08,970 --> 00:11:11,010
I can't stop hiccupping.

132
00:11:15,450 --> 00:11:17,310
My parents took me to see a doctor.

133
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:20,060
The doctor said it's stage fright,

134
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:22,360
caused by nervousness,

135
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:25,480
and that I have to overcome it myself.

136
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:33,360
Later, in middle school,

137
00:11:33,380 --> 00:11:36,240
I became an announcer
for the school radio station,

138
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:38,530
but that was all behind the scenes.

139
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:45,600
I really want to be like Senior Lin Hong,

140
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,120
and become a host

141
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:50,280
who can face a live audience.

142
00:13:24,450 --> 00:13:25,420
What's wrong with your hand?

143
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:26,750
It's nothing. Let's go.

144
00:13:29,920 --> 00:13:30,880
-Thanks for all your hard work.
-Okay.

145
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:32,240
-Go back and get some rest.
-See you then.

146
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:32,660
Bye-bye.

147
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:33,500
Bye-bye.

148
00:13:44,130 --> 00:13:44,970
Morning, Gu Han.

149
00:13:44,970 --> 00:13:45,500
Morning.

150
00:13:56,710 --> 00:13:57,360
Have you seen

151
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,800
anyone come by my desk?

152
00:13:58,900 --> 00:13:59,420
Nope.

153
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:04,060
Senior Fang Yu does good deeds
without taking credit.

154
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:05,190
He's so thoughtful.

155
00:14:06,910 --> 00:14:07,970
What are you doing?

156
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:10,500
I'm going to thank him.

157
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:13,900
The lecturer's here. Class is starting.

158
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:15,320
All right,

159
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:16,100
everyone.

160
00:14:16,150 --> 00:14:17,750
Last class,

161
00:14:17,930 --> 00:14:19,460
we divided you into groups,

162
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:21,960
but I'm not sure if everyone...

163
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:25,390
I heard dozens of people signed up
for the campus TV station this year.

164
00:14:25,390 --> 00:14:26,590
Think you can make it?

165
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:28,900
You underestimate me?

166
00:14:29,630 --> 00:14:31,280
I'll win first place and show you!

167
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:34,010
Each group must submit
one complete assignment.

168
00:14:35,150 --> 00:14:37,390
All right, this time, we're going to...

169
00:14:40,930 --> 00:14:43,090
[Tongue Twisters]
[Announcer and Host Training Manual]

170
00:14:49,090 --> 00:14:51,320
Speech sounds convey meaning and emotion

171
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:53,200
only when they flow naturally
in connected speech.

172
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,320
Clear articulation should be flexible,

173
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:56,480
relaxed,

174
00:14:56,560 --> 00:14:58,220
and smooth to aid expression.

175
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:01,160
Overly rigid,
syllable-by-syllable pronunciation...

176
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:02,560
-Study current affairs ....
-not only sounds affected...

177
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:04,400
-By reading the newspaper.
-But also feels unnatural.

178
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:06,360
The newspaper covers current affairs.

179
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:09,200
The vowel nucleus stands out prominently
within the syllable.

180
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,480
On the one hand,

181
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:12,230
it is the syllable's main vowel

182
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:14,320
and is pronounced
with the mouth most widely open.

183
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,040
The tip of the tongue curls back toward

184
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:18,680
or approaches the front
of the hard palate,

185
00:15:32,130 --> 00:15:33,420
allowing air to pass
through the narrow gap

186
00:15:33,420 --> 00:15:35,820
between the tongue tip
and the hard palate.

187
00:15:41,070 --> 00:15:43,860
[Training Pathways for Hosts'
Thinking and Language Skills]

188
00:15:44,220 --> 00:15:45,520
[Jiangcheng University
Campus TV Station Recruitment Drive]

189
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:46,820
[Preliminary Auditions]

190
00:16:11,050 --> 00:16:12,540
Xiangxiang, you came in first!

191
00:16:12,540 --> 00:16:14,340
You've made it to the next round.

192
00:16:15,620 --> 00:16:16,520
Let's go.

193
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:23,080
What's wrong? You're not happy?

194
00:16:23,710 --> 00:16:25,750
No. I was just thinking

195
00:16:26,170 --> 00:16:27,400
about the next round.
I'll have to introduce myself

196
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:28,920
and host in front of everyone.

197
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:30,440
There'll be judges

198
00:16:30,460 --> 00:16:32,060
and lots of people watching.

199
00:16:32,350 --> 00:16:33,710
I'm afraid I'll get nervous.

200
00:16:33,710 --> 00:16:35,390
It's okay. You can do it.

201
00:16:40,810 --> 00:16:42,080
See you at People's Square

202
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:42,960
at 5:30 p.m.

203
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:43,920
What's wrong?

204
00:16:44,890 --> 00:16:45,490
Nothing.

205
00:16:55,520 --> 00:16:56,850
You were waiting for me?

206
00:16:58,680 --> 00:17:00,540
Thanks for the book and the video.

207
00:17:02,250 --> 00:17:04,160
I happened to see it
when I was buying books online,

208
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:05,420
so I got it for you, too.

209
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:09,480
Still, I owe you a thank-you.

210
00:17:09,839 --> 00:17:11,400
I came first in the preliminary round,

211
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:13,160
and you helped me get there.

212
00:17:13,319 --> 00:17:14,440
I'll find a chance

213
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:16,240
to thank you properly sometime.

214
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:17,740
Keep your word.

215
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:20,000
Let's go.

216
00:17:32,270 --> 00:17:34,590
Basketball games often need

217
00:17:34,770 --> 00:17:35,910
professional MCs for informal events.

218
00:17:35,910 --> 00:17:37,030
Let's give it a try

219
00:17:37,110 --> 00:17:38,270
and see how you do today.

220
00:17:38,270 --> 00:17:40,430
What am I supposed to do here?

221
00:17:42,090 --> 00:17:44,690
Read the newspaper aloud
in front of everyone.

222
00:17:48,410 --> 00:17:50,470
Didn't you say you wanted to thank me?

223
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:52,120
Come on, man.

224
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:54,560
You want me to steal their jobs?

225
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:01,960
Hi, excuse me.

226
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:04,920
Could I borrow the speakers

227
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:05,830
and microphone?

228
00:18:05,830 --> 00:18:06,960
I'll pay you 300 yuan

229
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:08,210
to rent them for an hour. Is that okay?

230
00:18:08,210 --> 00:18:09,230
Go ahead. Go ahead.

231
00:18:09,230 --> 00:18:09,830
Thanks.

232
00:18:24,290 --> 00:18:25,810
Are you serious?

233
00:18:27,290 --> 00:18:28,950
Are you seriously doing this?

234
00:18:30,470 --> 00:18:31,530
Let's get started.

235
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:44,440
Recently,

236
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:47,260
good news has come
from Jiangcheng Wildlife Park!

237
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:51,520
The queen monkey has given birth
to three baby monkeys in quick succession.

238
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:53,200
The three babies are currently...

239
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:54,320
two...

240
00:18:55,810 --> 00:18:59,650
two males and one female...

241
00:19:01,410 --> 00:19:02,810
two females and one male!

242
00:19:12,410 --> 00:19:15,810
Recently, a couple in Jiangcheng
made a shocking discovery:

243
00:19:16,250 --> 00:19:18,160
the daughter they'd raised
and lived with for 13 years

244
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:19,400
was actually a boy.

245
00:19:19,650 --> 00:19:22,410
After a t-three-hour

246
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:23,520
operation,

247
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:25,080
the couple

248
00:19:25,410 --> 00:19:26,640
got their son back.

249
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:27,660
Is that good enough?

250
00:19:27,660 --> 00:19:28,380
Keep going.

251
00:19:33,050 --> 00:19:34,400
You've been through so much.

252
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:35,130
Stay strong.

253
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:39,640
I-I'm not...

254
00:19:39,770 --> 00:19:41,290
It's a misunderstanding.

255
00:19:43,940 --> 00:19:45,140
Don't let them get to you.

256
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:45,800
Keep going.

257
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:46,880
You can do it.

258
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:50,700
After all these years,

259
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,080
we've seen every kind of performance.

260
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:53,340
-S-Shan...
-Exactly.

261
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:54,520
-Shanqiao...
-But we've never seen anyone

262
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:56,180
deliver the news here before.

263
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:04,920
As—

264
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:06,760
Capture!

265
00:20:07,410 --> 00:20:08,010
The rook!

266
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:28,680
I've got you. Don't worry.

267
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,240
Shanqiao Village...

268
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:06,600
I've got you.

269
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:08,640
Don't worry.

270
00:21:25,050 --> 00:21:26,120
As the core development zone

271
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:28,600
of the Ten-Mile Lotus Pond,

272
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:32,220
Shanqiao Village has undergone
a dramatic transformation

273
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:34,220
in its environment.

274
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:36,640
Its annual income

275
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:39,440
has also grown from 90,000 yuan in 2015

276
00:21:40,080 --> 00:21:42,760
to 390,000 yuan

277
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:44,380
in 2019.

278
00:21:46,560 --> 00:21:47,440
Not bad!

279
00:21:48,720 --> 00:21:50,520
The security guards are coming!

280
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:51,320
Who's coming?

281
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:52,040
The security guards are coming!

282
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:52,760
Don't run!

283
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:54,480
-What do we do?
-Come on, let's go!

284
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:56,280
The security guards are coming!

285
00:21:56,410 --> 00:21:58,270
-Why are they running?
-Exactly.

286
00:22:22,590 --> 00:22:24,520
We can explain everything to them.

287
00:22:24,630 --> 00:22:26,360
What if they don't understand?

288
00:22:52,930 --> 00:22:54,260
Let's go back to campus.

289
00:22:55,090 --> 00:22:55,690
Let's go.

290
00:23:04,960 --> 00:23:06,110
[Jiangcheng University
Campus TV Station Recruitment Drive]

291
00:23:06,110 --> 00:23:07,270
[Second-Round Auditions]

292
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:09,160
In 1995, when the CBA

293
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:10,520
A-League was founded,

294
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:12,200
12 teams competed in it.

295
00:23:15,960 --> 00:23:17,560
All right, everyone, quiet down.

296
00:23:17,560 --> 00:23:19,490
The competition is about to begin.

297
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:22,400
Our first round will consist

298
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:25,480
of self-introductions
and a demonstration of stage presence.

299
00:23:25,480 --> 00:23:27,280
Let's welcome Contestant No. 1,

300
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:28,480
Zhou Xiangxiang.

301
00:23:38,600 --> 00:23:39,280
Thank you.

302
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:52,040
Hello, judges.

303
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:53,160
My name is Zhou Xiangxiang.

304
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:54,360
Hello, judges.

305
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:55,680
My name is Duan Xiaoyu.

306
00:23:55,840 --> 00:23:57,880
I'm Contestant No. 3, Zeng Mo.

307
00:23:57,920 --> 00:23:59,780
I'm Contestant No. 4, Zhang Ting.

308
00:23:59,800 --> 00:24:01,480
I'm a first-year student majoring

309
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:02,640
in Broadcasting and Hosting Arts.

310
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:04,020
I believe Chinese studies and broadcasting

311
00:24:04,020 --> 00:24:05,400
share a common purpose:

312
00:24:05,400 --> 00:24:06,400
using language

313
00:24:06,400 --> 00:24:07,920
to communicate with the world.

314
00:24:07,920 --> 00:24:09,200
This stage will be my first step

315
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:10,920
toward becoming a host.

316
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:13,760
To bring honor and glory
to the profession of hosting.

317
00:24:13,760 --> 00:24:15,920
That's what motivates me
to apply for this hosting position.

318
00:24:15,920 --> 00:24:16,560
Thank you.

319
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:23,720
Next is the second round:

320
00:24:24,160 --> 00:24:26,520
a mock hosting segment for
"Spring at Jiangcheng University."

321
00:24:26,520 --> 00:24:27,320
Please begin.

322
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:29,720
Tonight's
"Spring at Jiangcheng University"

323
00:24:29,720 --> 00:24:30,840
will feature two rounds of performances.

324
00:24:30,840 --> 00:24:32,360
After both rounds,

325
00:24:32,360 --> 00:24:34,640
this multi-day competition
will come to an end.

326
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:37,320
Tonight, we're honored
to welcome 5 special guests

327
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:39,120
to join the audience...

328
00:24:39,120 --> 00:24:41,280
To cast their votes for the contestants.

329
00:24:41,280 --> 00:24:42,000
So fake.

330
00:24:42,040 --> 00:24:43,720
Work on your fundamentals and try again.

331
00:24:43,720 --> 00:24:45,280
-Get off the stage!
-Get off the stage!

332
00:24:45,280 --> 00:24:46,600
Come down!

333
00:24:46,760 --> 00:24:49,000
With skills like that,
even I could do better.

334
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:50,360
Get off the stage already!

335
00:24:50,360 --> 00:24:52,020
What's wrong with what I said?

336
00:24:55,090 --> 00:24:55,890
So, next—

337
00:25:01,020 --> 00:25:02,500
Next...

338
00:25:16,800 --> 00:25:19,320
Don't waste time. Hurry up.

339
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:26,920
Look at me.

340
00:25:33,120 --> 00:25:34,850
Just keep your eyes on me, okay?

341
00:25:41,770 --> 00:25:43,050
Come on, keep going.

342
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:45,130
I've got you.

343
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:47,170
Don't worry.

344
00:25:52,790 --> 00:25:54,270
What's happening here

345
00:25:54,770 --> 00:25:57,010
reminds me of a book I read

346
00:25:58,300 --> 00:26:00,100
called "The Old Man and the Sea."

347
00:26:00,920 --> 00:26:01,880
The old man

348
00:26:01,900 --> 00:26:03,780
fought sharks and storms at sea

349
00:26:04,380 --> 00:26:07,340
to find the great fish

350
00:26:07,820 --> 00:26:09,220
he sought.

351
00:26:10,120 --> 00:26:10,920
In the end,

352
00:26:11,330 --> 00:26:13,170
he returned home.

353
00:26:14,650 --> 00:26:17,770
I feel

354
00:26:18,170 --> 00:26:19,630
just like that old man now.

355
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:22,560
I want to become a successful host.

356
00:26:23,840 --> 00:26:25,440
Your criticism and doubts

357
00:26:25,690 --> 00:26:27,290
are the storms I must face.

358
00:26:28,800 --> 00:26:30,750
Thank you all for helping me get here.

359
00:26:30,750 --> 00:26:32,190
I'd heard that

360
00:26:33,040 --> 00:26:35,090
if you dare to step
onto Jiangcheng University's stage,

361
00:26:35,090 --> 00:26:37,570
no stage will ever intimidate you again.

362
00:26:37,760 --> 00:26:40,440
-Bravo!
-Bravo!

363
00:26:41,280 --> 00:26:42,520
-Bravo!
-Well said!

364
00:26:42,520 --> 00:26:43,800
-Well said.
-Bravo!

365
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:46,000
-Thank you, everyone.
-Bravo!

366
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:49,480
-Bravo!
-Bravo!

367
00:26:49,480 --> 00:26:50,400
Amazing!

368
00:26:50,440 --> 00:26:51,280
Wonderful!

369
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:53,840
Thank you to all the contestants
for your wonderful performances today.

370
00:26:53,840 --> 00:26:55,880
Next, Mr. Zhang

371
00:26:56,320 --> 00:26:57,400
will announce

372
00:26:57,420 --> 00:26:59,300
the three contestants selected

373
00:26:59,640 --> 00:27:02,480
for the campus TV station.

374
00:27:03,160 --> 00:27:03,920
First,

375
00:27:05,720 --> 00:27:06,880
Duan Xiaoyu.

376
00:27:14,170 --> 00:27:14,970
Second,

377
00:27:15,360 --> 00:27:16,360
Zeng Mo.

378
00:27:20,940 --> 00:27:21,980
And third,

379
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:23,520
Zhou Xiangxiang.

380
00:27:53,250 --> 00:27:55,050
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

381
00:28:04,570 --> 00:28:06,370
Let me walk you back to your dorm.

382
00:28:12,470 --> 00:28:13,150
Let's go.

383
00:28:23,720 --> 00:28:24,400
Thanks.

384
00:28:25,660 --> 00:28:28,340
Your little lion seems
to work pretty well.

385
00:28:29,980 --> 00:28:32,440
You've improved through your own practice.

386
00:28:32,560 --> 00:28:34,020
Are you complimenting me?

387
00:28:42,660 --> 00:28:44,180
We're here. I'm off.

388
00:28:55,870 --> 00:28:56,870
Zhou Xiangxiang,

389
00:28:59,160 --> 00:29:00,420
you've got some nerve.

390
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:01,620
First, you used Senior Fang Yu

391
00:29:01,620 --> 00:29:03,000
to tutor you all the time.

392
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:04,080
Now

393
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:05,870
you've made it
onto the campus TV station,

394
00:29:05,870 --> 00:29:08,530
and you're already
trying to get close to Gu Han.

395
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:11,960
Senior Fang Yu only agreed to help you

396
00:29:11,960 --> 00:29:13,120
out of respect for Mr. Jiang.

397
00:29:13,120 --> 00:29:14,780
You really think he likes you?

398
00:29:18,570 --> 00:29:19,530
And don't think

399
00:29:19,760 --> 00:29:21,720
you've got Gu Han
wrapped around your finger now.

400
00:29:21,720 --> 00:29:23,320
Do you even know who Gu Han is?

401
00:29:23,480 --> 00:29:25,160
He's Jiangcheng University's heartthrob.

402
00:29:25,160 --> 00:29:26,320
He's handsome,

403
00:29:26,340 --> 00:29:27,800
comes from a well-off family,

404
00:29:27,800 --> 00:29:30,120
and has plenty of amazing girls
around him.

405
00:29:30,120 --> 00:29:31,560
Now look at yourself.

406
00:29:33,760 --> 00:29:36,560
Do you really think you're good enough
for Gu Han?

407
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:39,020
Tell me, exactly why am I

408
00:29:39,020 --> 00:29:40,740
not good enough for Gu Han?
